<Viewbox xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
  xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
  Stretch="Uniform"
  StretchDirection="Both">
  <Grid Width="1560" Height="920" TextElement.Foreground="#D8DCE0" TextElement.FontFamily="Roboto">
    <Grid.Resources>
      <Style x:Key="SlideArrowButton" TargetType="{x:Type Button}">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#8E969E"/>
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="58"/>
        <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Light"/>
        <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.58"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
          <Setter.Value>
            <ControlTemplate TargetType="{x:Type Button}">
              <Border Background="{TemplateBinding Background}">
                <ContentPresenter HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
              </Border>
              <ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                  <Setter Property="Background" Value="#28383B3F"/>
                  <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.82"/>
                </Trigger>
              </ControlTemplate.Triggers>
            </ControlTemplate>
          </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
      </Style>
    </Grid.Resources>

    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
      <RowDefinition Height="76"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="1"/>
      <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

    <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Text="INTRODUCTION" FontSize="28" FontWeight="SemiBold" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
    <Border Grid.Row="0" Width="76" Height="38" BorderBrush="#3E454B" BorderThickness="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,24,0">
      <TextBlock Text="2 / 3" FontSize="15" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
    </Border>
    <Rectangle Grid.Row="1" Fill="#3E454B" Margin="22,0"/>

    <Grid Grid.Row="2" Margin="0,10,0,0">
      <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
        <ColumnDefinition Width="122"/>
        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
        <ColumnDefinition Width="122"/>
      </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

      <Button Grid.Column="0" Width="96" Height="190" Style="{StaticResource SlideArrowButton}" Content="&lt;" Command="{Binding OpenFileCommand}" CommandParameter="campaigns/mare-nostrum-28/art/prologo_en.xml"/>
      <Button Grid.Column="2" Width="96" Height="190" Style="{StaticResource SlideArrowButton}" Content="&gt;" Command="{Binding OpenFileCommand}" CommandParameter="campaigns/mare-nostrum-28/art/prologo3_en.xml"/>

      <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Vertical">
        <Image Source="{Binding Assets[mn28_greenmarch]}" Height="410" Stretch="Uniform" HorizontalAlignment="Center"/>
        <TextBlock Text="The New Green March: crowds and Maghreb regimes united, moving north." FontStyle="Italic" FontSize="11" Foreground="#99A1A8" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,8,0,0"/>
        <TextBlock Text="The New Green March" FontSize="24" FontWeight="SemiBold" HorizontalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,20,0,12"/>
        <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="16" LineHeight="25" Foreground="#D0D4D8" Margin="150,0,150,0">
          Europe's hunger - energy, minerals, grain - has grown voracious, and the south has learned to hate it for that. From the Atlantic to the Nile, the governments of the Maghreb have united under a single banner: the <Span FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#8FBF7F">New Green March</Span>. They call it a tide of dignity; their arsenals, fresh from Moscow's factories, tell another story.
          <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
          They close routes. They board merchants. They claim waters and deposits Europe swore were its own. Every week a new line is crossed, and none is ever crossed back.
          <LineBreak/><LineBreak/>
          No one has declared war. No one needs to. <Span FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="#C98A6A">Two hungers stare at each other across a narrowing sea</Span>, and someone, very soon, will pull the trigger first.
        </TextBlock>
      </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
  </Grid>
</Viewbox>
